## Tool routing guide (quick reference)

| Question type | Dispatch to | Primary tools |
|---|---|---|
| "What is service X?" | code + docs | og (repo, API), ns (design docs), wp (owners) |
| "Who owns / runs X?" | code | wp (manager chain), ta (top committers) |
| "What tables does X use/produce?" | catalog | cy (metadata, lineage, ACL) |
| "How does X integrate with Y?" | code + catalog | og (code references), cy (shared tables/lineage) |
| "What's the research status of X?" | none | read research-index.md yourself in Step 1 |
| Full service research | all three | og + ta + wp + cy + ns |

## Rules

- Never re-research a `Complete` service — tell the user and offer to answer from existing docs
- Never write to the KB yourself — always route to scribe
- Never skip the architect synthesis step
- Never skip the critic review gate — scribe only receives critic-cleared findings
- Always read orientation files before routing — engineers need the "already cloned" context
